# Host Web API Executable

Use this pattern when creating or changing a Web API host executable named `<Prefix>.Host.Api`.

## Template Placeholders

Replace placeholders with names from the target solution:

| Placeholder | Example | Role |
|-------------|---------|------|
| `<Prefix>` | `Acme.Product` | Solution/project prefix |
| `HostConfiguration` | typed settings for the host | Main `appsettings` section |
| `FeatureConfiguration` | typed settings for an integration | Secondary `appsettings` section |
| `AddHostConfiguration()` | registration extension on `ContainerBuilder` | Registers `HostConfiguration` |
| `AddHost()` | registration extension on `ContainerBuilder` | Registers production host services |
| `HostCompositionRoot` | static composition class | Wires the production service graph |
| `HostRuntime` | runtime wrapper type | Resolved from DI; not injected into controllers |
| `IApplicationService` | primary domain abstraction | Injected into controllers |
| `ApplicationRequest` | domain input model | Mapped from HTTP request DTOs |
| `ApplicationController` | API controller | Thin HTTP adapter |

## Solution Structure

Host executables sit beside a shared composition library. Each executable has its own unit test project; shared host tests and integration tests live in separate projects.

```
src/
  Prefix.Host/                    # shared composition library (not executable)
    Configuration/
    Composition/
    DependencyInjection/
    Models/
  Prefix.Host.Api/                # Web API executable
    Program.cs
    appsettings.json
    Controllers/
    Properties/
  Prefix.Host.Console/            # console executable (see host-console.mdc)
  Prefix.Host.test/               # tests for the shared library only
  Prefix.Host.Api.test/           # tests for the API executable
  Prefix.Host.Console.test/       # tests for the console executable
  Prefix.Host.test.integration/   # end-to-end tests across executables
```

## Role In The Solution

- The API project is a **thin executable**. It exposes HTTP endpoints and bootstraps the host.
- Shared composition, factories, and `AddHost` registration live in `<Prefix>.Host`.
- The API project references **only** `<Prefix>.Host`. Do not add direct `<ProjectReference>` entries to domain or integration projects.

## Project Layout

- Project name: `<Prefix>.Host.Api`
- Test project name: `<Prefix>.Host.Api.test`
- Sdk: `Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web`

```
Prefix.Host.Api/
  Program.cs
  appsettings.json
  GlobalSuppressions.cs
  Controllers/
    ApplicationController.cs
    HealthController.cs
  Properties/
    launchSettings.json
```

```xml
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\Prefix.Host\Prefix.Host.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
```

## appsettings.json

Each executable carries its own `appsettings.json` with the sections its registration path requires:

- `Logging:Files:Path` — consumed by `RegisterLogConfiguration`
- `Host` (or the `HostConfiguration.SectionName` value) — consumed by `AddHostConfiguration`
- `Feature` (or the `FeatureConfiguration.SectionName` value) — consumed by `AddConfiguration<FeatureConfiguration>`

```json
{
  "Logging": {
    "Files": {
      "Path": "%TEMP%\\Prefix.Host.Api\\Logs"
    }
  },
  "Host": {
    "Setting": "value"
  },
  "Feature": {
    "Endpoint": "http://localhost:8080/",
    "Timeout": "00:05:00"
  }
}
```

## Wiring Chain

```
Program.RegisterConfiguration
  └─ RegisterLogConfiguration( "Logging:Files" )
  └─ AddHostConfiguration( HostConfiguration.SectionName )
  └─ AddConfiguration<FeatureConfiguration>( FeatureConfiguration.SectionName )

Program.RegisterServices
  └─ AddHost( configurationProvider )               # in Prefix.Host/DependencyInjection/
       └─ resolve HostConfiguration + FeatureConfiguration
       └─ HostCompositionRoot.RegisterProductionServices( builder )
            └─ external clients, domain services, tools
            └─ IApplicationService
            └─ HostRuntime

Program.RegisterWebServices
  └─ services.AddControllers()

ConfigurePipeline
  └─ app.MapControllers()

Controller action
  └─ inject IApplicationService + HostConfiguration (not HostRuntime)
```

- Configuration types are registered in `Program.RegisterConfiguration`.
- Production runtime services are registered only through `AddHost` in `<Prefix>.Host`.
- Controllers consume domain abstractions resolved from that graph.

## Program Bootstrap

- Follow `.cursor/rules/entry-points.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/host-composition.mdc`.
- Use an explicit `Program` class with a **public** `Main`, `RegisterConfiguration`, and `RegisterServices`.
- Use `WebApplication.CreateBuilder( args )` and `ConfigureDefaultHostApplication<Program>`.
- Wrap startup in `try/catch`, resolve `ILogger<Program>` from the Autofac root, and log startup failures before rethrowing.

```csharp
public static void Main( string[] args )
{
    ILogger? logger = null;

    try
    {
        var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder( args );

        builder.ConfigureDefaultHostApplication<Program>(
            string.Empty,
            RegisterConfiguration,
            RegisterServices,
            RegisterWebServices );

        var app = builder.Build();

        var container = app.Services.GetAutofacRoot();
        logger = container.Resolve<ILogger<Program>>();

        ConfigurePipeline( app );

        app.Run();
    }
    catch( Exception ex )
    {
        logger?.LogError( ex, "An error occurred while starting the application" );
        throw;
    }
}

public static void RegisterConfiguration( ContainerBuilder builder )
{
    builder.RegisterLogConfiguration( "Logging:Files" );
    builder.AddHostConfiguration( HostConfiguration.SectionName );
    builder.AddConfiguration<FeatureConfiguration>( FeatureConfiguration.SectionName );
}

public static void RegisterServices( ContainerBuilder builder,
                                     IAutofacConfigurationProvider configurationProvider )
    => builder.AddHost( configurationProvider );

private static void RegisterWebServices( IServiceCollection services )
    => services.AddControllers();

private static void ConfigurePipeline( WebApplication app )
    => app.MapControllers();
```

- `Program` wires bootstrap and the shared host library. Do not put business logic in `Program`.
- If the API grows feature-specific configuration or services, add `Infrastructure/` registration extensions colocated with that feature and call them from `RegisterConfiguration` / `RegisterServices`.

## Controllers

- Place controllers in `Controllers/`, not minimal API `Endpoints/` classes.
- Use `[ApiController]` and explicit route attributes.
- Inject `IApplicationService` and typed configuration such as `HostConfiguration`.
- Do **not** inject `HostRuntime` into controllers.
- Keep HTTP request/response models in `<Prefix>.Host/Models/` when they are shared with tests or multiple endpoints.
- Keep controllers thin: validate input, map to domain models (`ApplicationRequest`), call the application service, return `ActionResult<T>`.

## Forbidden

- Top-level statements.
- Delegating `Main` to a separate startup class.
- `InternalsVisibleTo` for test assemblies.
- Duplicating production composition that already belongs in `<Prefix>.Host`.
- Executable-specific tests in `<Prefix>.Host.test`; use `<Prefix>.Host.Api.test` instead.

## Tests

Test project layout:

```
Prefix.Host.Api.test/
  Configuration/
    ProgramConfigurationRegistrationTests.cs
    ProgramServiceRegistrationTests.cs
  Controllers/
    ApplicationControllerTests.cs
  Infrastructure/
    HostWebApplicationFactory.cs
```

Required composition tests:

- `ProgramConfigurationRegistrationTests` — call `Program.RegisterConfiguration`, resolve `HostConfiguration` and `FeatureConfiguration`, assert with `BeEquivalentTo`.
- `ProgramServiceRegistrationTests` — build `AutofacConfigurationProvider` with `Program.RegisterConfiguration`, call `AddConfigurationProvider`, call `Program.RegisterServices`, resolve `HostRuntime` and `IApplicationService`, verify the runtime exposes the same application service instance, assert configuration values.

Controller and HTTP tests:

- Place controller unit tests under `Controllers/`.
- Use a `WebApplicationFactory` in `Infrastructure/` when testing HTTP behavior.
- End-to-end scenarios that call real external services belong in `<Prefix>.Host.test.integration`.

Build test configuration with `AddJsonString()`, not `AddInMemoryCollection()`.
